# T21 — build context for `docker build`. Everything that only exists for
# local development, CI or secret-keeping is kept OUT of the build context:
# smaller layers, faster pushes, and no chance of a .env leaking into an
# image layer even if a Dockerfile bug tried to COPY . wildly.
.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
logs
*.log

# secrets and environment — never in an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem

# playwright/ coverage artifacts and local-only docs stay out; the tests/ TREE
# STAYS IN the context: client tests under src/ import tests/setup|helpers|msw,
# and `next build` type-checks src/** so it needs those files present.
# No secrets live in tests/; e2e runs against real browsers, not this image.
e2e
docs
scripts
audit-exceptions
vercel.json
.vercel
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# the build machinery itself (copied explicitly by the Dockerfile, not via .)
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
